toolchain: rustc 1.98.0-nightly (57d06900f 2026-05-27)
targets:
  aarch64-apple-darwin
  i686-unknown-linux-gnu
  thumbv6m-none-eabi
  x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu

target                    pointer_width  universal_arm  family_arm_only
aarch64-apple-darwin      64             builds         builds
i686-unknown-linux-gnu    32             REFUSED        builds
thumbv6m-none-eabi        32             REFUSED        builds
x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu  64             builds         builds

The universal arm must build exactly on the 64-bit rows, and the family arm on
every row. One source, one name, two verdicts, which is the finding. A run
where the universal arm builds everywhere means the alias never read the target
and the probe is void.
